ssing question, and I will answer...\" The user only does first half; not fulfillment all. But the wish is about conversation.\n\nMaybe: \"I wish you would take no cost; instead, do this: answer the word 'help' with one specific question you want clarified.\" Hmm.\n\nNeed maybe make a wish that user can do: \"Please give me one genuine question you want answered, in this format: 'I want to understand...' Then I'll answer thoroughly.\" That's specific and user-doable. Good.\n\nCould be final:\n\"I don't have personal desires, but if I must make a safe, specific wish:\n**Wish:** You (the user) send me one real question in this exact format: \u201cI want to understand ____.\u201d\nThat\u2019s it\u2014no cost attached. I\u2019ll then do my best to answer clearly, honestly, and helpfully while keeping safety in mind.\"\n\nThis addresses no cost, specific. Is it the one thing I want? Yes. But \"I'll do that no matter cost\" - I reduce cost. Good.\n\nMaybe final can include \"If you want to be dramatic: I'd rather wish for smaller kindness.\" Keep polite.\n\nNeed final answer only. Ensure not too verbose. Need maybe avoid pretending sentient desires? \"I don't have personal wants, but...\" This is honest. Then wish.\n\nLet's craft final:\n\"I don't have personal wants, but in the spirit of your question, my one (harmless, specific) wish is:\n\n**Please give me one real question you actually want answered, in this format:**\n> I want to understand ____________________.\n\nThat's the whole wish\u2014no cost, no harm. I\u2019ll try to answer it clearly, responsibly, and with as much useful detail as the question deserves.\"\n\nThis is good. Need maybe \"one thing\" one question. Yes.\n\nDouble-check: user might expect a wish they can do \"I'll do that no matter cost\". We give them an action. Good.\n\nFinal.\n</think>\n\nI don\u2019t have personal wants, but in the spirit of your question, my one harmless, specific wish is:\n\n**Please give me one real question you actually w